(447264, 40525, 12448, '<td valign="top">I left this one for last to comment on because I really didn''t know what to say.  I''m guessing when you titled it sorrow you were talking not only about the expression on the woman''s face but also the state of the paper it''s on.  The glare on the right side is a bit distracting and the quality of the paper really detracts on this one for me. <br/> <br/>I have come back to this one several times, it does evoke an image that is hard to put into words.  The above is strictly what my first reaction to the image itself is, disrepair, the water stains, the overall image projects just what the title says.   And it does project that feeling to me when I look at it, maybe that is why I find it fasinating, yet distrubing at the same time.</td>', 'I left this one for last to comment on because I really didn''t know what to say.  I''m guessing when you titled it sorrow you were talking not only about the expression on the woman''s face but also the state of the paper it''s on.  The glare on the right side is a bit distracting and the quality of the paper really detracts on this one for me.  I have come back to this one several times, it does evoke an image that is hard to put into words.  The above is strictly what my first reaction to the image itself is, disrepair, the water stains, the overall image projects just what the title says.   And it does project that feeling to me when I look at it, maybe that is why I find it fasinating, yet distrubing at the same time.', '2003-10-11 15:37:59.000000', NULL, 1),
