(448228, 40977, 11457, '<td valign="top">I want to thank everybody for the many comments I received. I had the idea for this shot while I was taking a shower (doh!), 20 minutes before the challenge submission deadline. I took 7-8 photos, changing light, position of the hand and so on. It was funny because I was alone and had to start the timer, actually lock myself inside the shower box, remove the marks I used as a reference on the glass, position the hand - and then start over. :) The shot I submitted was taken with a neon lamp inside the shower box. The shower box itself provided the orange tone, which I subsequently enhanced because I liked the "alarmed" mood it gave to the picture. I tried also blue tones and b&amp;w, but it didn''t really work (imho).<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-10-13 09:15:58.</i></td>', 'I want to thank everybody for the many comments I received. I had the idea for this shot while I was taking a shower (doh!), 20 minutes before the challenge submission deadline. I took 7-8 photos, changing light, position of the hand and so on. It was funny because I was alone and had to start the timer, actually lock myself inside the shower box, remove the marks I used as a reference on the glass, position the hand - and then start over. :) The shot I submitted was taken with a neon lamp inside the shower box. The shower box itself provided the orange tone, which I subsequently enhanced because I liked the "alarmed" mood it gave to the picture. I tried also blue tones and b&w, but it didn''t really work (imho).', '2003-10-13 01:39:11.000000', '2003-10-13 10:15:58.000000', 0),
(448240, 40975, 6870, '<td valign="top">Isn''t 13 an unlucky number? Nice work!</td>', 'Isn''t 13 an unlucky number? Nice work!', '2003-10-13 01:46:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(448243, 40948, 6870, '<td valign="top">Ursula, Ursula, Ursula . . . this has got to be one of the funkiest images of the challenge!</td>', 'Ursula, Ursula, Ursula . . . this has got to be one of the funkiest images of the challenge!', '2003-10-13 01:47:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(448246, 40733, 6477, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for the nice comments...<br/> <br/>This is a real women''s nightmare:)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-03-07 10:30:45.</i></td>', 'Thank you all for the nice comments... This is a real women''s nightmare:)', '2003-10-13 01:49:11.000000', '2004-03-07 10:30:45.000000', 0),
(448262, 40710, 10260, '<td valign="top">Now that the challenge is over, I wanted to say more about this photo.  This was a bonfire for the school spirit (homecoming game).  It was in a vacant lot, and I used the zoom to get it as close as I did.  I could have come closer, but didn''t want to intrude on the kids who were to the right of the fire.<br/> <br/> It does look fierce, doesn''t it? :) :)  The burning wood was pallets piled and set on fire.  I liked that it gave texture to the photo.  <br/> <br/> Thanks for all the comments.  I appreciate the time you took to comment and give ideas to make a better shot.</td>', 'Now that the challenge is over, I wanted to say more about this photo.  This was a bonfire for the school spirit (homecoming game).  It was in a vacant lot, and I used the zoom to get it as close as I did.  I could have come closer, but didn''t want to intrude on the kids who were to the right of the fire.  It does look fierce, doesn''t it? :) :)  The burning wood was pallets piled and set on fire.  I liked that it gave texture to the photo.    Thanks for all the comments.  I appreciate the time you took to comment and give ideas to make a better shot.', '2003-10-13 02:02:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(448266, 40972, 7778, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments.<br/> <br/>&gt; Firstrich1: So would I (love to know more about the sculpture). I found it on a Vancouver Beach well after sundown, apparently a transient piece. The fog was so thick, you couldn''t cut it, and the light you see in the photo is what my lens picked up. To my eyes it was pitch black.<br/> <br/>&gt; timmi: the raw shot, indeed, had a slightly orange hue to it. I desaturated and deliberately changed hues slightly to achieve a more subtle effect here.<br/> <br/>&gt; kiwiness: thanks for your consistent and generous comments, aber ''Verlauf'' ist männlich, as opposed to ''Helligkeit'', which is ''weiblich''. Ergo: ''der Helligkeitsverlauf''. (Will you ever forgive me for correcting your German grammar?) ;-)</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments. > Firstrich1: So would I (love to know more about the sculpture). I found it on a Vancouver Beach well after sundown, apparently a transient piece. The fog was so thick, you couldn''t cut it, and the light you see in the photo is what my lens picked up. To my eyes it was pitch black. > timmi: the raw shot, indeed, had a slightly orange hue to it. I desaturated and deliberately changed hues slightly to achieve a more subtle effect here. > kiwiness: thanks for your consistent and generous comments, aber ''Verlauf'' ist männlich, as opposed to ''Helligkeit'', which is ''weiblich''. Ergo: ''der Helligkeitsverlauf''. (Will you ever forgive me for correcting your German grammar?) ;-)', '2003-10-13 02:04:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(448269, 40893, 714, '<td valign="top">Boy, was it really that bad?  Can you really not tell what it is?  I like it, my kids and hubby like it.  Not sure why you all didn''t get it.  Try spending a few minutes looking at it.  No, it is not a picture of a picture. That is low, I would never do that.<br/> <br/>Any how thanks for the comments.</td>', 'Boy, was it really that bad?  Can you really not tell what it is?  I like it, my kids and hubby like it.  Not sure why you all didn''t get it.  Try spending a few minutes looking at it.  No, it is not a picture of a picture. That is low, I would never do that. Any how thanks for the comments.', '2003-10-13 02:05:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(448276, 40673, 1717, '<td valign="top">beautiful!  congrats, JJ!</td>', 'beautiful!  congrats, JJ!', '2003-10-13 02:09:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(448297, 40723, 11800, '<td valign="top">I didn''t comment on this one during the challenge because I wanted to see what you said about it. I could see that the child was completely absorbed in what she was doing and unaware of you taking her picture, but was wondering about the fading right side.<br/>The more I look at it, the more I like it. Very simple but strong also.</td>', 'I didn''t comment on this one during the challenge because I wanted to see what you said about it. I could see that the child was completely absorbed in what she was doing and unaware of you taking her picture, but was wondering about the fading right side.The more I look at it, the more I like it. Very simple but strong also.', '2003-10-13 02:16:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(448309, 40708, 5822, '<td valign="top">The only reason I think this didn''t get a ribbon (and a blue one at that) was because it takes on reality and isn''t expressive of the dreamlike and surrealistic images that most people have interpreted this challenge to be. To me, this is the superior image of the challenge! Hands down. Original idea that is so well executed. Like so many people that have already commented, you could feel her pain. Her pose and the lighting suggest that she can''t hide from the embarrassment as she tries to recoil into herself. Truly a shattered dream. So well done...bravo!</td>', 'The only reason I think this didn''t get a ribbon (and a blue one at that) was because it takes on reality and isn''t expressive of the dreamlike and surrealistic images that most people have interpreted this challenge to be. To me, this is the superior image of the challenge! Hands down. Original idea that is so well executed. Like so many people that have already commented, you could feel her pain. Her pose and the lighting suggest that she can''t hide from the embarrassment as she tries to recoil into herself. Truly a shattered dream. So well done...bravo!', '2003-10-13 02:25:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(448313, 40578, 51167, '<td valign="top">I thought this was one of the perfect photos for this challenge and I am very surprised that it didn''t score any higher.  The kind of blurriness and color are perfect for a dream.  The doll is really spooky and seems kind of like a ghost.  This is great.</td>', 'I thought this was one of the perfect photos for this challenge and I am very surprised that it didn''t score any higher.  The kind of blurriness and color are perfect for a dream.  The doll is really spooky and seems kind of like a ghost.  This is great.', '2003-10-13 02:28:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(448314, 40673, 4493, '<td valign="top">Nice photography. You''re ability to look to the simple things and pull out the essence of the shot amazes me. Great image, truely professional work.<br/> <br/>-danny</td>', 'Nice photography. You''re ability to look to the simple things and pull out the essence of the shot amazes me. Great image, truely professional work. -danny', '2003-10-13 02:31:06.000000', NULL, 0),
